  "scope": "Pooled automatic display calculation in C++/Python, all-Z-at-captured-T/C overlay and Apply in both ImGui hosts, scoped state/session/remapping and multi-plane typed manual threshold records.",
  "behavior": "All-Z scope estimates whole planes, renders the same inclusive interval on every Z at the captured T/C, and applies the numeric bounds to that frozen stack with the active 2D ROI repeated per plane. To Selection uses the captured plane. Scope is a consumed native preference. Typed API targets also accept ranges/positions and histogram ROI policies. Matched counts describe ROI members; ranges remain valid outside ROIs.",
  "compatibility": "Single-plane display and single-position command records retain version one. All-Z display adds version-two Boolean all_z. Multi-plane/range commands use schema two/manual_raw_inclusive_v2. Replay retains source/revision/selection validation and requires explicit destination rebinding. Z subsets preserve all-Z scope when the old anchor is removed. Variance/top-hat threshold reset recognizes an active non-anchor Z covered by all-Z state.",
  "resources": "Total target plane pixels including outside ROIs fit max_pixels (default 16 Mi pixels), not a per-plane multiplier. Scratch cap defaults to 128 MiB. Histogram calculation uses two scans and range/membership one more; legacy constant/mean shortcuts can use fewer. No concatenated pixel buffer. N+1-byte empty-result occupancy bitmap is admitted for Float64 max; plane/mask/histogram/manual-analysis scratch is included. Source/provider caches, captured geometry/bookkeeping, history, allocator overhead and process RSS remain external. Providers must remain immutable across reads.",
